IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap6-s2036a`

-- TESTS for snap6-s2036a.l4 (section 2036a, Nutrition education and obesity prevention grant program).
-- Every expected value is written here from the text quoted above the assertion, before the module was run.
-- JUST FALSE = "the text says no in its own words"; NOTHING = "not covered"; JUST TRUE = "the text says yes".

§ `Tests of section 2036a`

§§ `(a) eligible individual`
-- src:3144 | In this section, the term “eligible individual” means an individual who is eligible to receive benefits under a nutrition education and obesity prevention program under this section as a result of being—
-- src:3145 | (1) an individual eligible for benefits under—
-- src:3146 | (A) this chapter;
-- src:3147 | (B) sections 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4) of title 42; or
-- src:3148 | (C) section 1773(e)(1)(A) of title 42;
-- src:3149 | (2) an individual who resides in a community with a significant low-income population, as determined by the Secretary; or
-- src:3150 | (3) such other low-income individual as is determined to be eligible by the Secretary.
-- the arguments, in order: eligible under this chapter; under 42 U.S.C. 1758(b)(1)(A) and 1766(c)(4); under 42 U.S.C. 1773(e)(1)(A); resides in a community the Secretary found to have a significant low-income population; the Secretary found them another eligible low-income individual.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` (JUST FALSE) TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no limb true and every limb false: the definition "means", so the text says no.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a limb not supplied and none true: not covered; a limb not supplied but another true: decided without it.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` NOTHING FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(a) the individual is an eligible individual` NOTHING TRUE FALSE NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `(b) programs`
-- src:3152 | Consistent with the terms and conditions of grants awarded under this section, State agencies may implement a nutrition education and obesity prevention program for eligible individuals that promotes healthy food choices and physical activity consistent with the most recent Dietary Guidelines for Americans published under section 5341 of this title.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(b) the State agency may implement the program for the individual` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(b) the State agency may implement the program for the individual` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(b) the State agency may implement the program for the individual` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(b) the State agency may implement the program for the individual` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(b) the State agency may implement the program for the individual` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(c)(1) delivery`
-- src:3154 | (1) In general
-- src:3155 | State agencies may deliver nutrition education and obesity prevention services under a program described in subsection (b)—
-- src:3156 | (A) directly to eligible individuals; or
-- src:3157 | (B) through agreements with other State or local agencies or community organizations.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(1) the State agency may deliver the services this way` `s 2036a directly to eligible individuals` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(1) the State agency may deliver the services this way` `s 2036a through agreements with other State or local agencies or community organizations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(1) the State agency may deliver the services this way` `s 2036a in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(c)(2) State plans`
-- src:3159 | (A) In general
-- src:3160 | A State agency that elects to provide nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this subsection shall submit to the Secretary for approval a nutrition education State plan.
-- arguments: the State agency elects to provide the services; it has submitted a plan.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(A) the State agency has met the duty to submit a plan` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(A) the State agency has met the duty to submit a plan` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(A) the State agency has met the duty to submit a plan` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(A) the State agency has met the duty to submit a plan` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:3162 | A nutrition education State plan shall—
-- src:3163 | (i) identify the uses of the funding for local projects;
-- src:3164 | (ii) ensure that the interventions are appropriate for eligible individuals who are members of low-income populations by recognizing the constrained resources, and the potential eligibility for Federal food assistance programs, of members of those populations;
-- src:3165 | (iii) describe how the State agency shall use an electronic reporting system to—
-- src:3166 | (I) measure and evaluate the projects; and
-- src:3167 | (II) account for the allowable State agency administrative costs including for—
-- src:3168 | (aa) salaries and benefits of State agency personnel;
-- src:3169 | (bb) office supplies and equipment;
-- src:3170 | (cc) travel costs;
-- src:3171 | (dd) development and production of nutrition education materials;
-- src:3172 | (ee) memberships, subscriptions, and professional activities;
-- src:3173 | (ff) lease or rental costs;
-- src:3174 | (gg) maintenance and repair expenses;
-- src:3175 | (hh) indirect costs; and
-- src:3176 | (ii) cost of using publicly-owned building space; and
-- src:3177 | (iv) conform to standards established by the Secretary through regulations, guidance, or grant award documents.
-- the plan's four limbs, in order (i) to (iv).
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B) the plan contains what it shall` (`s 2036a what a plan contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B) the plan contains what it shall` (`s 2036a what a plan contains` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B) the plan contains what it shall` (`s 2036a what a plan contains` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B) the plan contains what it shall` (`s 2036a what a plan contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B) the plan contains what it shall` (`s 2036a what a plan contains` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:3168 | (aa) salaries and benefits of State agency personnel;
-- src:3169 | (bb) office supplies and equipment;
-- src:3170 | (cc) travel costs;
-- src:3171 | (dd) development and production of nutrition education materials;
-- src:3172 | (ee) memberships, subscriptions, and professional activities;
-- src:3173 | (ff) lease or rental costs;
-- src:3174 | (gg) maintenance and repair expenses;
-- src:3175 | (hh) indirect costs; and
-- src:3176 | (ii) cost of using publicly-owned building space; and
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a salaries and benefits of State agency personnel` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a office supplies and equipment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a travel costs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a development and production of nutrition education materials` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a memberships, subscriptions, and professional activities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a lease or rental costs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a maintenance and repair expenses` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a indirect costs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a cost of using publicly-owned building space` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(2)(B)(iii)(II) the cost is in a category the text lists` `s 2036a some other cost` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(c)(3) use of funds and consultation`
-- src:3180 | A State agency may use funds provided under this section for any evidence-based allowable use of funds identified by the Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service of the Department of Agriculture in consultation with the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention of the Department of Health and Human Services, including—
-- arguments: the use is evidence-based; the Administrator identified it.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the State agency may use the funds for the use` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the State agency may use the funds for the use` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the State agency may use the funds for the use` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:3181 | (i) individual and group-based nutrition education, health promotion, and intervention strategies;
-- src:3182 | (ii) comprehensive, multilevel interventions at multiple complementary organizational and institutional levels; and
-- src:3183 | (iii) community and public health approaches to improve nutrition.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the use is one of the examples the text gives` `s 2036a individual and group-based nutrition education, health promotion, and intervention strategies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the use is one of the examples the text gives` `s 2036a comprehensive, multilevel interventions at multiple complementary organizational and institutional levels` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the use is one of the examples the text gives` `s 2036a community and public health approaches to improve nutrition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(A) the use is one of the examples the text gives` `s 2036a some other use` EQUALS NOTHING
-- src:3185 | In identifying allowable uses of funds under subparagraph (A) and in seeking to strengthen delivery, oversight, and evaluation of nutrition education, the Administrator of the Food and Nutrition Service shall consult with the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture, and outside stakeholders and experts, including—
-- src:3186 | (i) representatives of the academic and research communities;
-- src:3187 | (ii) nutrition education practitioners;
-- src:3188 | (iii) representatives of State and local governments; and
-- src:3189 | (iv) community organizations that serve low-income populations.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator shall consult this person or body` `s 2036a the Director of the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator shall consult this person or body` `s 2036a the Director of the National Institute of Food and Agriculture` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator shall consult this person or body` `s 2036a representatives of the academic and research communities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator shall consult this person or body` `s 2036a nutrition education practitioners` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator shall consult this person or body` `s 2036a representatives of State and local governments` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator shall consult this person or body` `s 2036a community organizations that serve low-income populations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(3)(B) the Administrator shall consult this person or body` `s 2036a some other person or body` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(c)(4) notification`
-- src:3191 | To the maximum extent practicable, State agencies shall notify applicants, participants, and eligible individuals under this chapter of the availability of nutrition education and obesity prevention services under this section in local communities.
-- arguments: the person is an applicant, a participant or an eligible individual; notifying them is practicable.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(4) the State agency shall notify the person of the availability of the services` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(4) the State agency shall notify the person of the availability of the services` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(4) the State agency shall notify the person of the availability of the services` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(c)(5) coordination`
-- src:3193 | Subject to the approval of the Secretary, projects carried out with funds received under this section may be coordinated with the expanded food and nutrition education program or other health promotion or nutrition improvement strategies, whether public or privately funded, if the projects carried out with funds received under this section remain under the administrative control of the State agency.
-- arguments: the Secretary has approved the coordination; the projects remain under the administrative control of the State agency.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(5) the projects may be coordinated with other programs and strategies` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no approval: "Subject to the approval" is not a word that makes a failed condition a no.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(5) the projects may be coordinated with other programs and strategies` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(5) the projects may be coordinated with other programs and strategies` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the projects do not remain under the State agency's control: the "if" fails, whatever the approval.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(5) the projects may be coordinated with other programs and strategies` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(5) the projects may be coordinated with other programs and strategies` (JUST FALSE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(5) the projects may be coordinated with other programs and strategies` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `(c)(7) technical assistance`
-- src:3198 | (A) by identifying common challenges faced by entities described in paragraph (6) that participate in projects carried out with funds received under this section;
-- src:3199 | (B) by coordinating efforts to address those common challenges;
-- src:3200 | (C) by collecting and disseminating information on evidence-based practices relating to nutrition education and obesity prevention;
-- src:3201 | (D) by facilitating communication between and among grantees and subgrantees of funds received under this section;
-- src:3202 | (E) by assisting State agencies in creating or maintaining systems to compile program data; and
-- src:3203 | (F) by performing or assisting with other activities, as determined by the Secretary.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(7) the help is technical assistance the text lists` `s 2036a identifying common challenges faced by participating entities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(7) the help is technical assistance the text lists` `s 2036a coordinating efforts to address those common challenges` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(7) the help is technical assistance the text lists` `s 2036a collecting and disseminating information on evidence-based practices` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(7) the help is technical assistance the text lists` `s 2036a facilitating communication among grantees and subgrantees` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(7) the help is technical assistance the text lists` `s 2036a assisting State agencies in creating or maintaining systems to compile program data` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(7) the help is technical assistance the text lists` `s 2036a other activities, as determined by the Secretary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(7) the help is technical assistance the text lists` `s 2036a some other help` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `(c)(8) and (c)(9) the annual reports`
-- src:3206 | (A) the use of funds on the State agency’s program, including for each category of allowable State agency administrative costs identified in paragraph (2)(B)(iii)(II);
-- src:3207 | (B) a description of each project carried out by that agency under this subsection, including, with respect to the project, the target population, interventions, educational materials used, key performance indicators used, and evaluations made;
-- src:3208 | (C) a comprehensive analysis of the impacts and outcomes—
-- src:3209 | (i) of the project, including with respect to the elements described in subparagraph (A); and
-- src:3210 | (ii) to the extent practicable, of completed multiyear projects; and
-- src:3211 | (D) the status of any ongoing multiyear project.
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(8) the annual State report includes what it shall` (`s 2036a state report` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(8) the annual State report includes what it shall` (`s 2036a state report` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2036a(c)(8) the annual State report includes what it shall` (`s 2036a state report` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
